  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 78c39ca0aa3b4c60ad7cb11e9f4cf262, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialTopic_Intro
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Features.Tutorial.Data.TutorialTopicData
  <Title>k__BackingField: Intro
  <Chapters>k__BackingField:
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Welcome!
    <Description>k__BackingField: Thanks for playing Medieval Merchant. Your goal
      is to build a profitable trade network by buying and selling goods between
      towns and helping them grow over time.
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: c709834b8c40f154eadafcdd233b5c4f, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Trading & Prices
    <Description>k__BackingField: Goods can be bought and sold in towns. Prices are
      driven by supply and demand. Scarce goods sell for more, abundant goods sell
      for less. World events and town state can further influence prices.
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: eb9eea30894c9254d857dacffb175916, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Towns at a Glance
    <Description>k__BackingField: Each town produces certain goods based on nearby
      resources. Supplying towns with what they lack helps them grow and unlock better
      production and trade opportunities.
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: f98f770fb6e4dec4482fbe90558c34d0, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Winning and Losing
    <Description>k__BackingField: To win you need to satisfy all win conditions and
      manage to not trigger any losing condition.
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 843a113f39c8d1c4ab58c8014f647e47, type: 3}
  - <Title>k__BackingField: Good Luck!
    <Description>k__BackingField: 'That is all for now :)

      You will learn more
      as you play. Enjoy the journey!'
    <Image>k__BackingField: {fileID: 2800000, guid: f3fd06d3747dcc54890b0bcdbfd25640, type: 3}
